{"D:\\wt\\smblessing\\vlog\\smblessing\\voz\\b011_t8.wav": {"text": "Tell them their seat is still warm for you. Every October our church has homecoming. Everyone who ever belonged comes back for a potluck and there are three tables of pies. People who have not spoken in years end up sitting side by side. The verse for that day is from Psalm 133. Behold, how good and how pleasant it is for brethren to dwell together in unity. It is the shortest sermon I know and the pies do most of the talking. The thing I pray at homecoming is simple. Bring us home to each other, Lord. Most of us have one relative or one old friend that we drifted away from over a dish or a sentence or a year nobody can remember. Think of that person this week. You don't have to fix the whole thing. Reach out to them and bring the pie. Some mornings, even now, I set out two cups without thinking. Nine years now and I still do it. Grief doesn't go away.", "words": [{"w": " Tell", "s": 0.0, "e": 0.22}, {"w": " them", "s": 0.22, "e": 0.38}, {"w": " their", "s": 0.38, "e": 0.7}, {"w": " seat", "s": 0.7, "e": 0.9}, {"w": " is", "s": 0.9, "e": 1.18}, {"w": " still", "s": 1.18, "e": 1.42}, {"w": " warm", "s": 1.42, "e": 1.72}, {"w": " for", "s": 1.72, "e": 2.02}, {"w": " you.", "s": 2.02, "e": 2.38}, {"w": " Every", "s": 2.72, "e": 3.06}, {"w": " October", "s": 3.06, "e": 3.56}, {"w": " our", "s": 3.56, "e": 3.9}, {"w": " church", "s": 3.9, "e": 4.18}, {"w": " has", "s": 4.18, "e": 4.54}, {"w": " homecoming.", "s": 4.54, "e": 5.12}, {"w": " Everyone", "s": 5.68, "e": 6.08}, {"w": " who", "s": 6.08, "e": 6.42}, {"w": " ever", "s": 6.42, "e": 6.76}, {"w": " belonged", "s": 6.76, "e": 7.14}, {"w": " comes", "s": 7.14, "e": 7.46}, {"w": " back", "s": 7.46, "e": 7.78}, {"w": " for", "s": 7.78, "e": 8.06}, {"w": " a", "s": 8.06, "e": 8.24}, {"w": " potluck", "s": 8.24, "e": 8.78}, {"w": " and", "s": 8.78, "e": 9.12}, {"w": " there", "s": 9.12, "e": 9.32}, {"w": " are", "s": 9.32, "e": 9.52}, {"w": " three", "s"